    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WiuK3EYFXxFgYTNmw2q6y3)_\n\n## What\n\nNew module `sp-reading-sidenotes` (ui), doc `docs/tangles/ui/sp-reading-sidenotes.org`, tests `tests/sp-reading-sidenotes-test.el`.\n\n- In `sp-reading-mode`, each see-also footnote (`[fn::[[id:...][Concept]]]`) shows as a small number in the text and as a Tufte-style sidenote in the right margin. The file is not changed (overlays only).\n- Footnotes come from `sp-see-also-parse-buffer` (#366), no second parser.\n- The note starts on the line of its number, wraps in the margin (`sp-reading-sidenote-margin`, 30 columns), and moves down if it would overlap the previous one. It is redone on window changes, text scale and edits (idle timer).\n- Turns on/off with `sp-reading-mode` (`sp-reading-sidenotes`), or alone with `C-c w s`. The right margin is widened while it is on and restored afterwards. Narrow windows keep the plain footnotes.\n- `M-x sp-reading-sidenotes-export` exports the note with `ox-tufte` (installed via `use-package` + Elpaca `:ensure`) and opens the HTML.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Stacked on #366** (base branch `claude/project-thread-7yi4nb`); retarget to `main` after it merges.\n- `ox-tufte` is an export backend, so it cannot draw in an Emacs window: the on-screen sidenotes use the Emacs margin display, and ox-tufte makes the matching HTML. It turns every inline footnote into a sidenote, not only see-also ones.\n- The frame is not resized for the wider margin; the text column narrows instead.\n- No CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).\n\n## Tested\n\n- 13 ERT tests (Emacs 29.3 batch, all pass): scanning through the parser, link text, margin line wrapping, overlay creation/removal, no overlap, narrow window, margin set/restore, following reading mode.\n- A manual ox-tufte export of a footnote produced a `sidenote-number` label.\n- Not seen in a real GUI frame: the actual look, wrapping, and `vertical-motion` placement on screen are untried. The vault and DEVONthink are not involved.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9asHrTP3hoa4foozS)_",
